      "comment": "BOLTA (3) won five on end before a nose defeat in this grade before the break. He's since trialled strongly in the year off and Faithfull sticks from his latest effort. Looks primed to return on a positive note and with things suiting, he can land the knockout blow. ONEMORETWOMANY (2) is the race-fit danger after two narrow thirds this campaign, the latest as favourite when beaten just under a length, and his record at this track and distance is a clear positive. LUCKEE FLORAN (6) rises from a BM58+ win, but he put the race away by a length and a half and gets weight relief, so he can hold a competitive spot despite the stronger grade.  GOLD KEEPER (4) is better than he showed last start and can bounce back to form.",
